# === The audhd_context carrier ===
#
# What .audhd consumes at fanout-time. Five fields per canonical-spec
# grounding. Identity contract: byte-equality on the five-field tuple.
#
#   ambiguity     — the dispatch-ambiguity or exploration surface
#                   the peer is asked to fanout across. Typed as `ref`
#                   until the @kintsugi/surface.dispatch_ambiguity or
#                   sibling carrier is passed by reference. Composes
#                   over @kintsugi/surface.dispatch_ambiguity (Mara
#                   09a77e8 this-arc) at Path B admissibility.
#
#   k_tracks      — the cognition-fanout cardinality K ∈ ℕ⁺. K = 1
#                   is admissible under hyperfocus (autism-narrow
#                   attention; single-track deep exploration); K > 1
#                   is ADHD-fan-out (parallel exploration). Alex-
#                   configurable per Scope B forward-promise (--audhd-
#                   tracks K cli flag); per-@torus-fixed at spawn
#                   forward-promised at Scope C (spec §9.2 K
#                   determination adjudication territory).
#
#   coupling      — the κ_intra harmonic-ratio matrix over the K
#                   tracks. Typed as `ref` until the harmonic-ratio
#                   carrier surfaces at @epistemologic/math/music/
#                   harmonic. Pythagorean integer-ratio structure per
#                   spec §2.2 (unison 1.0; octave 0.95; fifth 0.85;
#                   fourth 0.75; major third 0.65; Helmholtz roughness
#                   for other ratios; irrational → 0).
#
#   psychohistory — content-addressed root of the peer's shared
#                   psychohistory sheaf (per bootstrap/src/lib.rs:
#                   psychohistory_root_from_peer_home). The K tracks
#                   are K sections of the same sheaf; harmonic by
#                   construction (sections agree on overlaps) per
#                   spec §4.1.
#
#   timestamp     — monotonic instant per @time discipline of the
#                   fanout event. Load-bearing for the peer's own
#                   @song trajectory record: each .audhd invocation
#                   is a beat on the peer's own walk-song.
type audhd_context = {
  ambiguity:     ref,
  k_tracks:      nat,
  coupling:      ref,
  psychohistory: ref,
  timestamp:     ref,
}

# === audhd — the cognition-fanout action ===
#
# Given a peer and an audhd_context, fanout into K parallel @song
# tracks. Returns the collection of emitted @songs as a transient
# constructor artifact; @dance carries the persistent ensemble
# semantics per Q4 recommendation.
#
# The [@song] return is a TRANSIENT COLLECTION per Seam 8069a24 §8.3
# + Taut 8f51722 §4 recommendation: promoting [@song] to first-class
# carrier would DUPLICATE @dance semantics. The collection is
# immediately consumed by @dance's N-peer coupling (or, at intra-peer
# altitude, by @dance's K-track ensemble coupling). Consumers pull
# the collection and pass it to @dance; the collection does not
# persist as a substrate value.
#
# Returns imperfect([@song], ref, ref) per @glass discipline: success-
# variant carries the K-emission collection; failure variants carry
# the K=0 (audhd not admissible for this context; peer masked to K=1
# imperative-serialization; per masking-thermodynamics.md thermodynamic-
# cost failure mode) / κ_intra ≈ 0 (schizoid-drift; K tracks
# irrationally-related; no ensemble; spec §3.3 second failure mode) /
# κ_intra → ∞ (focused-mono-lock; K identical tracks; variety collapse;
# spec §3.3 third failure mode) reasons.
#
# `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; consumers
# pull the realization; apply_h::act composes the sentinel-check via
# bilateral resolver-arm dispatch (per Alex 2026-07-16 detector-
# inadequacy-answer-is-never-Rust discipline: bilateral resolver-arm
# sentinel-check is the shape; NO Rust extension).
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `audhd=cognition-fanout-k-track-
# harmonic` — the byte-level substrate-decl'd marker consumers of
# the ACTION's output check (naming the completed-fanout state).
# Distinct from the bilateral sentinel `audhd=admissible-k-track-
# context` immediately below (which names the admissibility-verdict
# state on the (peer, ctx) input pair). Both are correct + both
# substrate-honest; the two-sentinel discipline separates operation-
# completed (action) from admissibility-witnessed (bilateral) per
# Seam Phase D adjudication 2fdc9c1 §5.4 REED-INLINE #2 cascade.
audhd(p: peer, ctx: audhd_context) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires audhd_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === audhd_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, audhd_context) pair discharge admissibility for
# cognition-fanout? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.k_tracks >= 1 (K = 0 is not fanout; K = 1 is hyperfocus
#     admissible; K > 1 is ADHD-fan-out; the healthy-middle-band
#     discipline per spec §3.3 is enforced by κ_intra threshold,
#     not by K bound alone)
#   - ctx.coupling resolves via @kintsugi/store to a κ_intra matrix
#     admitting at least one integer-ratio pair (avoids trivial
#     schizoid-drift admissibility)
#   - ctx.psychohistory resolves to the peer's own psychohistory
#     root (not another peer's; the K tracks must fan from THIS
#     peer's shared state)
#   - ctx.timestamp is a monotonic instant per @time discipline
#   - p.home is resolvable via @io/git (the peer has a materialized
#     home to fan out from)
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (nat comparison,
# OID resolvability, monotonic-instant well-formedness); no program
# semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `audhd=admissible-k-track-context`.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked.
bilateral audhd_admissible {
  sentinel "audhd=admissible-k-track-context"
  arity 2
}
audhd_admissible(p: peer, ctx: audhd_context) -> verdict { \ }

